Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.41,0:00:04.19,Default,Shinozaki,0,0,0,,Narita's father hired his friend \Nto cause the accident and harm you.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:04.19,0:00:05.32,White-Standard,Sign,0,0,0,,{\an8\pos(320,20)\bord4}"...caused by the father's friend"
Dialogue: 0,0:00:05.32,0:00:06.69,georgia,Sign,0,0,0,,{\bord0}Saneatsu Narita's Medical Records
Dialogue: 0,0:00:07.04,0:00:09.80,Default,Shinozaki,0,0,0,,He likely sacrificed your kidney \Nin return for a Prime Right.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:10.20,0:00:11.41,Black-Standard,Sign,0,0,0,,{\bord0\frz-1\pos(277,18)\b0}Narita Saneatsu\N\Nis the key
Dialogue: 0,0:00:12.33,0:00:14.60,Default,Shinozaki,0,0,0,,Saneatsu Narita is the key to everything!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:21.71,0:00:24.42,Show Title,Title,0,0,0,,{\fad(250,0)\pos(320,110)}Tasuketsu: Fate of the Majority
Dialogue: 0,0:00:24.42,0:00:27.09,Show Title,Title,0,0,0,,{\fad(250,0)\pos(320,110)}Tasuketsu: Fate of the Majority
Dialogue: 0,0:00:27.09,0:00:31.76,Show Title,Title,0,0,0,,{\fad(250,0)\pos(320,110)}Tasuketsu: Fate of the Majority
Dialogue: 0,0:01:48.21,0:01:51.38,Italics,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,Dad was a member of the Camp...
Dialogue: 0,0:01:51.98,0:01:55.01,Italics,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,The person who hit me was Dad's friend...
Dialogue: 0,0:01:55.70,0:01:58.03,Italics,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,So Mom's death was just collateral damage.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:59.02,0:02:02.27,Italics,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,I'm the key to Tasuketsu.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:04.60,0:02:07.96,Default,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,I can't stay with everyone else.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:09.49,0:02:12.24,Default,Ryuta,0,0,0,,Ha! Quit kidding around.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:12.64,0:02:13.99,Default,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,I'm not kidding anyone.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:14.46,0:02:18.87,Default,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,I've done my best to survive and \Ndefeat the Emperor with you guys,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:19.18,0:02:25.37,Default,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,but it turns out I was putting you \Nin harm's way for no good reason.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:25.68,0:02:27.54,Default,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,I don't deserve to be with you.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:27.88,0:02:30.34,Default,Ryuta,0,0,0,,Are you serious?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:30.34,0:02:32.49,Default,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,You'll be fine without me.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:32.49,0:02:33.68,Default,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,You have Saaya.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:33.68,0:02:35.97,Default,Saaya,0,0,0,,You're our leader.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:35.97,0:02:38.32,Default,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,Saaya, we agreed that you—
Dialogue: 0,0:02:42.40,0:02:46.70,Default,Omi,0,0,0,,I... I've always been scared of other people.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:46.70,0:02:49.36,Default,Omi,0,0,0,,It's always just been me by myself, but...
Dialogue: 0,0:02:51.15,0:02:53.90,Default,Omi,0,0,0,,Saneatsu, you called me a friend.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:54.41,0:02:58.79,Default,Omi,0,0,0,,The only reason I'm able to talk with \Neveryone today is because of you, Saneatsu.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:59.20,0:03:00.36,Default,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,Omi...
Dialogue: 0,0:03:00.98,0:03:02.23,Default,Ryuta,0,0,0,,I...
Dialogue: 0,0:03:03.00,0:03:05.44,Default,Ryuta,0,0,0,,I'm only alive right now because of you!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:05.44,0:03:07.71,Default,Ryuta,0,0,0,,'Cause you're the most important \Nperson in the world to me!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:08.45,0:03:09.34,Default,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,Ryuta...
Dialogue: 0,0:03:09.34,0:03:10.63,Default,Kazuhiko,0,0,0,,And I'm...
Dialogue: 0,0:03:10.63,0:03:14.63,Default,Kazuhiko,0,0,0,,I'm no good at anything, but \Nyou've always counted on me.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:14.63,0:03:16.16,Default,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,Kazuhiko...
Dialogue: 0,0:03:16.16,0:03:20.04,Default,Gobo,0,0,0,,When I was ready to give up, \NKazuhiko lit a fire in me.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:20.55,0:03:24.71,Default,Gobo,0,0,0,,But aren't you the one \Nwho helped him do that, for real?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:24.71,0:03:30.81,Default,Eren,0,0,0,,I'm still here because you showed me\N the way when I wanted to run off.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:32.33,0:03:34.03,Default,Rika,0,0,0,,You know...
Dialogue: 0,0:03:34.03,0:03:37.15,Default,Rika,0,0,0,,Omi may be the one who saved my life,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:37.15,0:03:41.08,Default,Rika,0,0,0,,but I believe in you as someone \NIsshiki put her trust in.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:42.49,0:03:43.59,Default,Shinozaki,0,0,0,,Narita...
Dialogue: 0,0:03:44.47,0:03:47.00,Default,Shinozaki,0,0,0,,In my desperation to survive, \NI became reckless.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:47.00,0:03:50.07,Default,Shinozaki,0,0,0,,But you and Sudo helped \Nsomeone as shallow as me.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:50.91,0:03:55.51,Default,Souma,0,0,0,,I owe him my life, but you're the one \Nwho shook some sense into him.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:57.01,0:03:59.55,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,{\i1}You're{\i0} the man Ryohei Sudo trusted.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:00.01,0:04:03.93,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,I almost feel bad for only \Nhaving one life I can owe you.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:08.41,0:04:09.50,Default,Saaya,0,0,0,,Saneatsu...
Dialogue: 0,0:04:10.39,0:04:13.77,Default,Saaya,0,0,0,,Even we were caught up in \Nsimply making it out of Tasuketsu alive,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:14.14,0:04:17.86,Default,Saaya,0,0,0,,you were the first to decide \Nto defeat the Emperor.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:17.86,0:04:21.99,Default,Saaya,0,0,0,,Ever since that day, we've \Nbeen committed to that goal.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:21.99,0:04:25.49,Default,Saaya,0,0,0,,And that conviction gives me \Nstrength every day.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:26.29,0:04:29.00,Default,Saaya,0,0,0,,Strength brought to me by your words.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:29.48,0:04:31.63,Default,Saaya,0,0,0,,We're here thanks to you.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:32.67,0:04:37.34,Default,Saaya,0,0,0,,You brought us together.\N You're what holds us together.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:39.33,0:04:42.54,Default,Saaya,0,0,0,,So please, don't say that you'll leave.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:43.36,0:04:45.90,Default,Saaya,0,0,0,,You're already a part of us, Saneatsu.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:54.57,0:04:55.69,Default,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,You guys...
Dialogue: 0,0:04:57.97,0:04:58.57,Default,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,Thank—
Dialogue: 0,0:04:58.57,0:05:00.03,Default,Ryuta,0,0,0,,Boom!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:00.03,0:05:01.60,Default,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,What's that for?!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:01.60,0:05:04.85,Default,Ryuta,0,0,0,,If you've got time to cry,\N then plan how we'll see Ren Iruga!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:04.85,0:05:07.03,Default,Ryuta,0,0,0,,Come on, let's go!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:07.03,0:05:10.46,Default,Omi,0,0,0,,Ryuta-kun really can't stand\N a somber atmosphere...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:10.46,0:05:11.79,Default,Souma,0,0,0,,Ren Iruga?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:11.79,0:05:13.34,Default,Shinozaki,0,0,0,,You know him, Souma?!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:13.34,0:05:14.96,Default,Souma,0,0,0,,Yeah, from the Camp...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:15.39,0:05:19.34,Default,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,Ren Iruga came from the Camp. He's \Nthe owner of the Prime Right of Division.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:19.34,0:05:20.82,Default,Souma,0,0,0,,That's right!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:20.82,0:05:23.84,Default,Souma,0,0,0,,I heard about someone who\N pulled the strongest Prime Right.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:24.27,0:05:28.31,Default,Souma,0,0,0,,Ren Iruga was supposedly their best friend.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:28.31,0:05:29.98,Default,Shinozaki,0,0,0,,I never heard that.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:30.26,0:05:33.41,Default,Souma,0,0,0,,It was just a rumor among \Na small group of people.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:33.41,0:05:36.29,Default,Souma,0,0,0,,Researchers caught wind and \Nput it to bed pretty soon after...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:36.29,0:05:39.24,Default,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,Iruga was best friends with \Nthe owner of the Obedience Right?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:39.24,0:05:42.80,Default,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,How can anyone \Ndetermine what's "strongest"
Dialogue: 0,0:05:42.80,0:05:44.64,Default,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,without knowing every \NRight in the first place?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:44.64,0:05:47.49,Default,Ryuta,0,0,0,,It'd be possible if you know \Nwhat's inside every envelope.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:48.01,0:05:52.75,Default,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,Exactly. The rumor was started \Nby the person who helped my dad...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:52.75,0:05:55.83,Default,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,the owner of the Prime Right \Nof Transillumination.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:56.84,0:06:01.88,Default,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,No one else could know the contents \Nof each envelope or see through rumors.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:01.88,0:06:04.55,Default,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,And if any rumors happened to be true, \Nthey'd have to put an end to it.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:04.55,0:06:06.55,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,So that's where Ren Iruga comes in.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:06.55,0:06:09.52,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,He'd be the only clue to the \Nowner of the Obedience Right.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:11.27,0:06:14.21,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,That's why the Camp kept \Na close eye on Ren Iruga,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:14.21,0:06:19.01,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,while also being careful \Nnot to press him too hard.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:19.01,0:06:22.24,Default,Ryuta,0,0,0,,Doesn't that sound like \Nthe researcher is behind it all?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:22.53,0:06:25.70,Default,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,Right. That researcher is likely Mido.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:25.70,0:06:28.29,Default,Rika,0,0,0,,This is way too hard for me to follow!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:28.29,0:06:30.04,Default,Rika,0,0,0,,Fill me in on the conclusion later.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:30.99,0:06:32.57,Default,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,Change of plans!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:33.25,0:06:36.08,Default,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,Be it Iruga or Mido, \Nwe'll lure one of them out.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:37.08,0:06:38.76,Default,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,Preferably Mido.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:38.76,0:06:42.44,Default,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,If my assumption is right, Mido's Prime Right \Nis something along the line of succession.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:42.84,0:06:46.59,Default,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,Even if it comes to armed conflict, \Nwe have Ryuta and Souma.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:47.07,0:06:51.10,Default,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,But if Iruga or both of them show up, \Nlet's try for a peaceful discussion.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:51.10,0:06:53.08,Default,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,If that's not possible, we'll retreat.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:53.46,0:06:54.70,Default,Ryuta,0,0,0,,Sounds good.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:54.70,0:06:57.06,Default,Rika,0,0,0,,His Prime Right is bad news.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:57.37,0:06:59.15,Default,Saaya,0,0,0,,How will we lure them out?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:59.15,0:07:01.14,Default,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,We'll need Gobo's help.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:02.03,0:07:05.68,Default,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,I'm thinking of drawing them here \Nusing his Presentation Right.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:06.69,0:07:09.00,Default,Gobo,0,0,0,,So it's my time to shine \Nwith these powers of mine,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:09.00,0:07:10.74,Default,Gobo,0,0,0,,banned at the Institution of Darkness...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:10.74,0:07:12.21,Default,Souma,0,0,0,,Gobo?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:12.21,0:07:15.71,Default,Shinozaki,0,0,0,,Institution? Is he from the Camp too?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:16.49,0:07:19.75,Default,Gobo,0,0,0,,Very well. In times of need, leave it to—
Dialogue: 0,0:07:18.69,0:07:20.69,Default-Top,Shinozaki,0,0,0,,That reminds me! Speaking of tonight!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:20.69,0:07:23.96,Default,Gobo,0,0,0,,Hey! I'm delivering my line here, for real!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:24.36,0:07:26.34,Default,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,What's happening tonight, Sensei?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:26.34,0:07:29.68,Default,Shinozaki,0,0,0,,We'll be able to narrow down the Emperor's \Nwhereabouts from tonight's announcement!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:29.68,0:07:30.55,Default,Saaya+Saneatsu,0,0,0,,What?!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:30.83,0:07:34.02,Default,Shinozaki,0,0,0,,The Emperor selects Designated \NAreas out of the 23 wards.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:34.41,0:07:36.48,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,As they mentioned at the \Nbeginning of Tasuketsu.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:36.78,0:07:40.29,Default,Shinozaki,0,0,0,,According to Sudo, these areas \Nare determined by two principles.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:40.29,0:07:42.30,Default,Shinozaki,0,0,0,,Depending on the next area,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:42.30,0:07:44.38,Default,Shinozaki,0,0,0,,we can narrow it down\N to one or two locations.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:44.38,0:07:46.66,Default,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,Are you sure?!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:46.66,0:07:47.82,Default,Shinozaki,0,0,0,,Take a look at this.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:48.56,0:07:50.21,Default,Shinozaki,0,0,0,,It's a map of the 23 wards.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:51.17,0:07:54.02,Default,Shinozaki,0,0,0,,If we mark the areas we've \Npassed through so far...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:54.66,0:07:56.66,Comp big-an8,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fad(500,1)\pos(61,308)\1a&H3D&}Suginami
Dialogue: 0,0:07:54.66,0:07:56.66,Comp big-an8,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fad(500,1)\pos(195,262)\1a&H3D&}Nakano
Dialogue: 0,0:07:54.66,0:07:56.66,Comp big-an8,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fad(500,1)\pos(100,141)\1a&H3D&}Nerima
Dialogue: 0,0:07:54.66,0:07:56.66,Comp big-an8,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fad(500,1)\pos(292,82)\1a&H3D&}Itabashi
Dialogue: 0,0:07:54.66,0:07:56.66,Comp big-an8,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fad(500,1)\pos(410,84)\1a&H3D&}Kita
Dialogue: 0,0:07:55.26,0:07:56.34,Default-Top,Shinozaki,0,0,0,,It looks like this.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:57.86,0:07:59.12,Default,Saaya,0,0,0,,They're adjacent?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:59.55,0:08:02.80,Default,Shinozaki,0,0,0,,Exactly. Sudo concluded from our path so far
Dialogue: 0,0:08:02.80,0:08:06.88,Default,Shinozaki,0,0,0,,that we're moving in a clockwise \Ndirection, spiraling inwards.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:07.14,0:08:10.22,Default,Souma,0,0,0,,But some wards have \Nmore than one adjacent ward.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:10.22,0:08:13.28,Default,Shinozaki,0,0,0,,Right. Suginami has Nerima and Nakano.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:10.22,0:08:13.43,Comp big-an8,Sign,0,0,0,,{\1a&H3D&\pos(152,240)}Suginami
Dialogue: 0,0:08:10.22,0:08:13.43,Comp big-an8,Sign,0,0,0,,{\1a&H3D&\pos(498,257)}Nakano
Dialogue: 0,0:08:10.22,0:08:13.43,Comp big-an8,Sign,0,0,0,,{\1a&H3D&\pos(145,83)}Nerima
